165 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H2/P 91 0 R/T(On 15th June 2026, Mayor Khan launched a \2437 million plan to tackle the "dark blizzard of disinformation" which he claimed is giving people a false impression of London. An accusation that looks like a confession.)/E(On 15th June 2026, Mayor Khan launched a \2437 million plan to tackle the "dark blizzard of disinformation" which he claimed is giving people a false impression of London. An accusation that looks like a confession.)/Pg 12 0 R/K[6]>>
endobj

166 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H2/P 91 0 R/T(Just five days earlier, he had announced the positive results of the first year of his "bold new plan" to tackle fare evasion. If there are 100 people in your Tube carriage then 5 of them didn't pay; in total these free riders cost London \243190m per year so it's a problem that needs tackling. But it doesn't feel like it's getting better, so is the Mayor right to say his plan is working?)/E(Just five days earlier, he had announced the positive results of the first year of his "bold new plan" to tackle fare evasion. If there are 100 people in your Tube carriage then 5 of them didn't pay; in total these free riders cost London \243190m per year so it's a problem that needs tackling. But it doesn't feel like it's getting better, so is the Mayor right to say his plan is working?)/Pg 12 0 R/K[7]>>
endobj

167 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H2/P 91 0 R/T(On his new plan, the Mayor claimed that "new figures show that it's working" when in fact they showed it made no difference: fare evasion was unchanged at 3.5% of journeys. Nor was the plan new: I've discovered it was a 2025 relaunch of a 2023 plan. And it was the opposite of "bold", as it had relaxed the fare evasion target from 1% to 1.5% and pushed the deadline back 6 years. Conveniently putting it beyond his term in office.)/E(On his new plan, the Mayor claimed that "new figures show that it's working" when in fact they showed it made no difference: fare evasion was unchanged at 3.5% of journeys. Nor was the plan new: I've discovered it was a 2025 relaunch of a 2023 plan. And it was the opposite of "bold", as it had relaxed the fare evasion target from 1% to 1.5% and pushed the deadline back 6 years. Conveniently putting it beyond his term in office.)/Pg 12 0 R/K[8]>>
endobj

168 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 91 0 R/E(Figure 1 \204 Mayor of London tweet on fare evasion crackdown, 10 June 2026, claiming "new figures show that it's working".)/Pg 12 0 R/K[9]>>
