522 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H3/P 102 0 R/T(The composition matters. The improvement in the headline rate since 2022/23 is driven almost entirely by the Underground's fall from its post-pandemic spike \(6.7% to around 5%\) and the Elizabeth line. Bus evasion has risen steadily \(1.9% to 2.6%\), tram evasion remains around 7\2058%, and Underground evasion rose again in 2025/26 to 5.0%. That's one unpaid journey in twenty.)/E(The composition matters. The improvement in the headline rate since 2022/23 is driven almost entirely by the Underground's fall from its post-pandemic spike \(6.7% to around 5%\) and the Elizabeth line. Bus evasion has risen steadily \(1.9% to 2.6%\), tram evasion remains around 7\2058%, and Underground evasion rose again in 2025/26 to 5.0%. That's one unpaid journey in twenty.)/Pg 23 0 R/K[66]>>
endobj

523 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H3/P 102 0 R/T(On TfL's own pre-pandemic estimates, evasion today is roughly double its 2018/19 level on most modes: buses 1.6% then against 2.6% now; the Underground 2.5% then against 5.0% now; the DLR 0.56% then against 4.0% now.)/E(On TfL's own pre-pandemic estimates, evasion today is roughly double its 2018/19 level on most modes: buses 1.6% then against 2.6% now; the Underground 2.5% then against 5.0% now; the DLR 0.56% then against 4.0% now.)/Pg 23 0 R/K[67]>>
endobj

