688 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H2/P 105 0 R/T(Against this, the London Assembly Transport Committee was told that before 2022/23 TfL "did not consistently track or measure levels of fare evasion". The record shows a consistent, published, multi-modal measurement regime with named survey months, sample sizes and methodology, running from the mid-2000s until at least 2019/20 \(the January 2020 FOI reports survey results to December 2019\). The gap is 2020\2052022; the silence about 2017\2052019 remains unexplained \204 years for which an update was requested, promised in writing, and never delivered.)/E(Against this, the London Assembly Transport Committee was told that before 2022/23 TfL "did not consistently track or measure levels of fare evasion". The record shows a consistent, published, multi-modal measurement regime with named survey months, sample sizes and methodology, running from the mid-2000s until at least 2019/20 \(the January 2020 FOI reports survey results to December 2019\). The gap is 2020\2052022; the silence about 2017\2052019 remains unexplained \204 years for which an update was requested, promised in writing, and never delivered.)/Pg 26 0 R/K[14]>>
endobj

